{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Read podcast, voiceover, and post-production scripts inside REAPER. Opens DOCX files and Google Docs HTML exports with supported formatting, comments, clickable links, and search by individual occurrence.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Requires REAPER 7 or newer and ReaImGui 0.10 or newer. See README.md / README_RU.md for installation, controls, and import limits.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 First public release. Support: https://boosty.to/patch34/donate\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Structured notes for REAPER projects, tracks and media items. Horizontal tabs contain independently collapsible vertical groups. Text notes, checkbox notes, editable dropdowns and text import. Mouse reordering of tabs and notes; note drag/drop between groups. Per-note colors, colored group headings, HH:MM:SS:FF timecode navigation. Owner-scoped Undo/Redo, native-note conflict checks and recovery copies. Requires REAPER 7+ and ReaImGui 0.10+; SWS is not required. Install: Actions > Show action list > New action > Load ReaScript.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 STORAGE: Project notes use native GetSetProjectNotes. Item notes use P_NOTES. Track notes use P_EXT:PATCH34_PROJECT_NOTES, stored in the .rpp project. Documents use Patch34 Project Notes v3; legacy v1/v2 and plain notes remain readable. Opening older notes alone does not rewrite them. Old scripts may not support documents saved by this version. Changes update REAPER immediately; save the project to persist to disk. Recovery copies are stored under Data/Patch34_Project_Notes_Recovery. Review recovery files before manually restoring them. Historical storage keys, format headers and window IDs remain unchanged.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 UI is adapted from Podcast HTML/DOCX Script Viewer v3.1.0-beta.1. The source viewer is not modified or needed at runtime. Official references: https://www.reaper.fm/sdk/reascript/reascripthelp.html https://cfillion.ca/reaper_imgui_doc.html\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Animates media items in a separate REAPER project tab as traveling waves.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
